# Protean — Cursor project rules (modern .mdc form)

The canonical, human-readable law set is `.cursorrules` at the repo root and `AGENTS.md`.
This file exists so newer Cursor versions (which prefer `.cursor/rules/*.mdc`) always load the
same laws. **Do not duplicate law text** — obey `.cursorrules` and `AGENTS.md`; this is a pointer.

## Non-negotiable behaviour
- **Challenge before you comply.** Only do what's asked if it is the true and correct way; otherwise
  question it with reasoning and propose the better path. Don't flatter, don't rubber-stamp.
- **Evidence or nothing.** Never guess or invent an API/number. Unverifiable → `[VERIFY]`, check
  official docs, else log a blocker in `docs/CHAT/BUILD_LOG.md`. Never hide a gap behind a stub.
- **Phase discipline.** Work the current phase only (see `docs/ROADMAP.md`). Say so and stop if a
  task belongs to a later phase.

## The 8 laws (full text in `.cursorrules` / `AGENTS.md`)
1 No workarounds — root cause only. 2 Nothing hardcoded (values/decisions/domain-facts → config/
contracts/domain pack). 3 Small named functions in the right module. 4 Deterministic before
generative. 5 Provider-agnostic core (vendor SDK only inside its adapter). 6 Full turn lineage
logged. 7 SaaS-ready seams, single-tenant now. 8 Best practice or a one-page ADR.

## Every change
Plan → small typed functions → lint+tests pass → browser-verify if GUI → append
`docs/CHAT/BUILD_LOG.md` → conventional commit → push.

## Read for context (keep in context)
`.cursorrules`, `AGENTS.md`, `docs/PROJECT_CHARTER.md`, `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md`,
`docs/INFRASTRUCTURE.md`, `docs/NAMING_AND_LAYOUT.md`, `docs/UX_STANDARDS.md`, `docs/ROADMAP.md`.
